From: OHOS PC porting <noreply@atomgit.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Accept flat-layout ncursesw (single ncurses.h + libncursesw.a)

configure.ac assumes a distro ncurses layout: the wide-character
build installs <ncursesw/ncurses.h> and links -lncursesw, while the
narrow build uses <ncurses.h> and -lncurses.  The Conan ncurses
package installs one FLAT header (include/ncurses.h already contains
the wide API: cchar_t, add_wch, ...) and one library (libncursesw.a).
With that layout upstream's probes fail: AC_CHECK_HEADERS
(ncursesw/ncurses.h) -> no, the ncursesw loop iteration is skipped
(header != yes), the ncurses iteration finds no libncurses.a either,
and AC_SEARCH_LIBS(initscr) dies with "You need ncurses!".

Fix the detection itself: in the ncursesw iteration, accept the flat
<ncurses.h> as the wide header when the subdirectory header is
missing.  AC_CHECK_LIB then probes addch/add_wch in libncursesw.a
(both present), wide_ncurses=ncursesw, AC_SEARCH_LIBS resolves
initscr to -lncursesw exactly as on a distro system, and
HAVE_WIDE_NCURSES / USE_NCURSES_W are defined as before.
includes.h keeps <ncursesw/ncurses.h> under USE_NCURSES_W when
HAVE_NCURSESW_NCURSES_H is set (distro layout) and falls back to the
flat <ncurses.h> otherwise — that single header IS the wide one.
No shim directory, no fake defines.

Upstream-URL: https://sourceforge.net/p/lcsgame/code/HEAD/tree/trunk/
---
 configure.ac   |  8 ++++++++
 src/includes.h |  7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index 56c189b..47301d1 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -26,7 +26,15 @@ AC_CHECK_HEADERS([stdlib.h string.h sys/time.h unistd.h ncurses.h ncursesw/ncurs
 for lib in ncurses ncursesw; do
    if test "$lib" = ncursesw; then
       name="NCURSES_W"
-      header="$ac_cv_header_ncursesw_ncurses_h"
+      # Distro layout: <ncursesw/ncurses.h>.  Flat layout (Conan
+      # ncurses): a single <ncurses.h> at the include root that
+      # already contains the wide API (cchar_t, add_wch, ...); accept
+      # it as the wide header when the subdirectory one is missing.
+      if test "$ac_cv_header_ncursesw_ncurses_h" = "yes"; then
+         header="yes"
+      else
+         header="$ac_cv_header_ncurses_h"
+      fi
    else
       name="NCURSES"
       header="$ac_cv_header_ncurses_h"
diff --git a/src/includes.h b/src/includes.h
index 620c0c6..ab3df98 100644
--- a/src/includes.h
+++ b/src/includes.h
@@ -156,7 +156,13 @@ const int lowestloadscoreversion=31203;
       #if defined(USE_NCURSES)
          #include <ncurses.h>
       #elif defined(USE_NCURSES_W)
-         #include <ncursesw/ncurses.h>
+         #if defined(HAVE_NCURSESW_NCURSES_H)
+            #include <ncursesw/ncurses.h>
+         #else
+            /* Flat ncurses package: the single ncurses.h IS the
+               wide-character header (defines cchar_t, add_wch, ...). */
+            #include <ncurses.h>
+         #endif
       #else
          #error "You must define either USE_NCURSES or USE_NCURSES_W."
       #endif
